import detector

samples = {
    "borderline": "Time management matters more than people admit, especially now that work moves as fast as it does. If you're organised you hit deadlines, and you're less frazzled doing it. A few things actually help. Prioritise — work out what genuinely matters and do that first. Cut the interruptions; notifications wreck focus and the damage is worse than it feels at the time. And take breaks, short ones, often.",
    "clearly_ai": "The importance of effective time management cannot be overstated in today's fast-paced work environment. Professionals who develop strong organizational habits are better positioned to meet deadlines and reduce stress. There are several key strategies that can help individuals improve their productivity. First, prioritization is essential. By identifying the most important tasks and addressing them first, workers can ensure that critical objectives are met. Second, minimizing distractions plays a significant role. Setting aside dedicated blocks of time for concentrated work is widely considered beneficial. Finally, regular breaks are important for maintaining performance.",
    "clearly_human": "I didn't sleep. Not properly, anyway — I lay there listening to the boiler tick and thinking about the thing I'd said to Marcus at the pub, which was stupid, and which he will absolutely bring up again. Twice now. So: coffee, and the long way round to work, and a plan. The plan lasted until about ten past nine, when Priya asked how the weekend was and I said \"fine\" in the voice that means it wasn't, and she put her mug down and looked at me. That's the trouble with Priya. She notices.",
}

for label, text in samples.items():
    score = detector.model_signal(text)
    print(f"{label:>15}: {score}")